item.description:
This is a new cross-programme role created to help techUK and its members explore, shape and accelerate the responsible deployment of autonomous systems and drones across these markets. The Programme Manager will work horizontally across techUK's defence, national security and justice & emergency services programmes, identifying shared opportunities and challenges, joining up members and stakeholders who might otherwise operate in silos, and building techUK's profile as a leading voice on autonomous systems for the public sector.
Key Responsibilities
Present techUK as the voice of the technology industry to government departments, regulators and key stakeholders, whilst building new relationships and furthering programme priorities. Support the development, implementation and communication of techUK's autonomous systems activities in a way that meets the needs of existing and potential new members;
Work across techUK's defence, national security and justice & emergency services programmes to identify, develop and exploit opportunities to deploy autonomous systems and drones, joining up members and stakeholders across these markets;
Lead the development, implementation and management of projects, white papers, workshops and events that aim to resolve shared challenges between the technology industry and its public sector customers on the adoption and deployment of autonomous systems;
Lead the set-up and execution of programme events, briefings and meetings, and support the activities of relevant Groups, Forums and working groups spanning the autonomous systems agenda;
Engage with key regulators and enablers including the Military and Civil Aviation Authorities and relevant government bodies, to understand and help shape the frameworks that govern the deployment of drones and autonomous systems;
Promote techUK's autonomous systems work through insights, opinions, social media and marketing activities;
Liaise with other techUK programme teams to identify and exploit cross-fertilisation opportunities with programmes, ensuring alignment between the defence, national security and justice & emergency services programmes and the wider organisation;
Support the work of various relevant member councils, maintaining liaison with participating members.
A full version of the job role can be found on our website linked below.
Closing Date
: 14 August 2026
Interview/Start Dates
Candidates who are shortlisted will be contacted promptly to arrange an interview.
Application Details
Apply for the role by clicking on the below link and submitting your CV for consideration:
https://careers.techuk.org/postings/0e0b209f-beed-4891-b684-8a0cc3872d74?utm_medium=job_board&utm_source=W4MP
Website
:
http://techuk.org

We are currently recruiting for a Client Relationship Executive to support the development and delivery of sponsorship for our programme of online public policy conferences.
This role is focused on research, organisation, coordination and relationship management, rather than high-volume sales. It will suit someone who is highly organised, comfortable working across multiple projects at once, and interested in public policy, business and current affairs.
The successful candidate will play a key role in researching and identifying potential sponsors for new conference topics, managing inbound enquiries, and ensuring existing sponsors are supported effectively from initial engagement through to event delivery.
This role would ideally suit a recent graduate or someone looking for their second role in a professional environment.
Responsibilities include:
• Researching organisations, sectors and individuals that may be interested in sponsoring specific conference topics, and proactively suggesting new commercial leads;
• Approaching potential sponsors and responding promptly and professionally to inbound enquiries;
• Managing sponsor relationships once secured, acting as a key point of contact and ensuring commitments are delivered smoothly;
• Coordinating with internal teams on sponsor requirements, materials and conference logistics;
• Tracking leads, sponsor activity and outcomes accurately across multiple events;
• Preparing sponsorship documentation, packages and bespoke proposals as required.
We are looking for:
• Excellent research skills and the ability to identify relevant organisations for different policy and business themes;
• Strong organisational, planning and tracking skills, with close attention to detail;
• An interest in current affairs, public policy and the business environment;
• Clear, professional written and verbal communication skills;
• The ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines simultaneously, working independently and as part of a team;
• Confidence using CRM systems, spreadsheets or similar tracking tools would be beneficial.
Closing Date
: 1 September 2026
Interview/Start Dates
Application Details
To apply, please email your CV and covering letter (including current salary and why you believe you would be suitable for the role) to
recruitment@westminsterforumprojects.co.uk
Website
:
https://www.westminsterforumprojects.co.uk/

Help to turn inside knowledge into a powerful lever for corporate accountability.
There are millions of people going to work each day with a sense that they are, in some way, working against the world they want to live in. They may know what needs to change and have ideas about how change could happen, but lack a safe and credible route through which to act.
Inside Track creates that route. We build confidential movements of senior professionals inside powerful industries, giving them protected spaces to share what they see. Their insight helps key stakeholders understand the cultures, structures, norms and incentives creating negative social and environmental outcomes, and apply targeted pressure to redress these.
The Senior Campaigns Manager plays a key role in this work. You will work across multiple industries, providing strategic input on the timing, medium, and narrative of campaigns, ensuring that they resonate with their target audience and effectively create the environment for change to happen.
This is not a standard campaigning role. Each industry group and each issue raised will demand an entirely different approach and may have a different pathway to impact, which will likely be complex, indirect, and long-term. You will need to be a highly strategic thinker, bold in vision and comfortable in uncertainty.
Who this could suit
We are looking for someone with significant experience in building campaigns with a successful NGO, who can take our impact to the next level. Specifically, we are hoping you will have:
• at least 5 years’ relevant professional experience, with at least 2 years’ managing campaigns for a successful NGO;
• a track record of creating impact through compelling campaigns;
• a strategic eye, with strong judgement on power, timing, tone and risk;
• strong creative intuition, with a sense of what medium and message appeals to what group;
• an understanding of when and how media engagement creates value;
• the ability to communicate complex, sensitive and high-leverage work clearly;
• a serious and demonstrable commitment to social and environmental change;
• comfortable self-starting and working through uncertainty without a complete playbook;
• discretion when handling sensitive work;
• warm, curious, resilient, high conviction and low ego.
Closing Date
: 24 August 2026
Interview/Start Dates
Application closing time: 12pm
Interviews: Early September
Start date: As soon as possible
Application Details
Please send a CV and Cover Letter to
recruitment@insidetrack.org.uk
Website
:
http://www.insidetrack.org.uk/
